Patch-Id: ASTRA-0016
Title: Keep the declared PRInt32 return type in NSPR's Windows socket check
Tier: P2
OS: windows
Upstream-Files: nsprpub/pr/src/md/windows/w95sock.c
Intent: clang 23 promotes -Wincompatible-pointer-types to an error. Firefox 160 already declares DWORD rvSent (prsocket.c), DWORD bytes (w95io.c), u_long result and DWORD dwBytes (w95sock.c), and ntmisc.c now passes a temp variable to GetExitCodeProcess, so those hunks were removed on 2026-11-23 (upstream fixed them). One narrowing remains: _MD_SocketAvailable declares u_long result and returns it from a PRInt32 function. The cast restores the declared API type; the value is unchanged.
Risk: low (u_long and PRInt32 are both 32-bit on Windows)
Test: `forge lint`; `mach build --jobs 7` on Windows gets past config/external/nspr/pr
Verified-On: 153.6.0
Removal-Plan: drop entirely if Firefox makes this cast or the build is clean without it; the other four sites were satisfied by 160. Re-check after a base bump with `git -C engine diff FETCH_HEAD -- nsprpub/pr/src/io/prsocket.c nsprpub/pr/src/md/windows/ntmisc.c nsprpub/pr/src/md/windows/w95io.c nsprpub/pr/src/md/windows/w95sock.c`
---
diff --git a/nsprpub/pr/src/md/windows/w95sock.c b/nsprpub/pr/src/md/windows/w95sock.c
--- a/nsprpub/pr/src/md/windows/w95sock.c
+++ b/nsprpub/pr/src/md/windows/w95sock.c
@@ -110,8 +110,8 @@
     u_long result;
 
     if (ioctlsocket(fd->secret->md.osfd, FIONREAD, &result) < 0) {
         PR_SetError(PR_BAD_DESCRIPTOR_ERROR, WSAGetLastError());
         return -1;
     }
-    return result;
+    return (PRInt32)result;
 }
